{{- $vm := get .fleet.exe (index .fleet.work 0) -}}
# Managed by chezmoi (WSL work laptop only). The work network only lets 443
# and SSH out, so https://{{ $vm }}.exe.xyz:<port>/ doesn't load here. This
# forwards the dev-server ports (fleet.ports in .chezmoidata/fleet.yaml) from
# the work VM to localhost; Windows apps reach them through WSL's localhost
# forwarding.
[Unit]
Description=Forward dev-server ports from {{ $vm }} to localhost

[Service]
# WSL's ssh, not ssh.exe: the key registered with exe.dev lives in WSL.
# A port already taken locally is skipped instead of failing the tunnel.
ExecStart={{ lookPath "ssh" | default "/usr/bin/ssh" }} -N \
  -o BatchMode=yes -o ExitOnForwardFailure=no \
  -o ServerAliveInterval=30 -o ServerAliveCountMax=3 \
{{- range .fleet.ports }}
  -L {{ . }}:localhost:{{ . }} \
{{- end }}
  {{ $vm }}.exe.xyz
Restart=always
RestartSec=15

[Install]
WantedBy=default.target
